\subsection{Research attempt}
\paragraph{Model, date and investigated scope.}
OpenAI GPT-6 Astra (configured model \texttt{gpt-6-astra}), ultra reasoning; generated 11 October 2026. Derived pure-gauge linearized tensor solutions, including separated apparent growth, to test the correct geometric quotient in mode stability.

\paragraph{Sources and literature check.}
Read the full supplied definition, catalogue wording, source qualifications and listed references for 30006049. No fresh status or novelty search was performed. The argument below proves its auxiliary statements directly and does not import an unverified external theorem.

\paragraph{Why raw tensor modes contain false instabilities.} Write the geometric Einstein operator as \(\mathcal E(g)=\operatorname{Ric}(g)+\Lambda g\) in the convention of the source. For any smooth diffeomorphism \(\Phi\), tensor covariance gives \(\mathcal E(\Phi^*g)=\Phi^*\mathcal E(g)\). If \(\mathcal E(g)=0\) and \(\Phi_s\) is the local flow of a vector field \(X\), differentiating at \(s=0\) gives
\[
 D\mathcal E_g(\mathcal L_Xg)=\mathcal L_X\mathcal E(g)=0.
\]
Thus every infinitesimal coordinate change supplies a linearized tensor solution.
\paragraph{Separated growing gauge fields.} On a stationary coordinate patch choose \(X=e^{\sigma t}Y(x)\), \(\sigma>0\), with smooth spatially supported \(Y\). Since the background is time independent, \(\mathcal L_Xg\) is also proportional to \(e^{\sigma t}\) and generically nonzero. Taking the spatial support away from horizon and asymptotic boundaries avoids artificial local boundary singularities. This produces apparent growing solutions of the ungauged coordinate equation, but they represent zero geometric perturbation after quotienting by infinitesimal diffeomorphisms.
\paragraph{First physical-mode gap.} The calculation explains why componentwise scalar estimates or absence of raw growing tensors is not the requested statement. One must prove that every admissible nondecaying tensor mode in the full subextremal range is gauge or a permitted family-parameter variation, with the actual horizon conditions and regularity. No classification of the quotient kernel is proved here, and no estimate uniform near excluded degenerate horizons is asserted. The first unresolved step is precisely that geometric kernel analysis beyond the small-parameter regimes.

\paragraph{Verification and adversarial audit.}
